From 1c1685b31bddc205a409e417d8a51886feab48ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] SableOS: Battery health and Charging & protection in
 Settings > Battery

Adds two rows to the Battery page, in the design's order (Battery
usage, Battery health, Charging & protection, Battery saver):

* Battery health: each fact shows its value with source and confidence,
  or an explicit "Not reported" / "Not yet verified on this device".
  Facts come from the sticky ACTION_BATTERY_CHANGED broadcast and
  BatteryManager properties only; no sysfs. A local history chart
  (Today / 24 hours / 7 days) with keyboard inspection sits below.
  History is sampled on the existing hourly battery-usage job and when
  a Battery screen opens: no new alarm, wakelock or service.
* Charging & protection: read-only capability discovery. Charge limit,
  adaptive and overnight charging render as unavailable rows that stay
  focusable; thermal protection and the reported charging policy are
  status text. LineageOS charging control and charging speed are hidden
  while the Sable gate (BH6) is closed. Unavailable controls are indexed
  for search only with an explicit "(not available on this device)".
* The Battery usage row summary lists the top system consumers from
  BatteryUsageStats with the start of the accounting window.
* Android's ungated Battery information row is hidden, and its page
  dropped from the search index, in favour of the gated health page.
* Keyboard: type-ahead over titles and aliases (U, H, C, B), MoveHome,
  MoveEnd, PageUp, PageDown, "/" or Ctrl+K for search, and a
  high-contrast focus ring, on the Battery, usage, health and charging
  screens.

The device capability profile is read from
/system_ext/etc/sable/battery/<ro.sable.profile.id>.conf; without one
everything stays unavailable.
